  <bpmn:process id="Process_35" name="Recipe and Bill of Materials Maintenance" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-35 and catalog process ownership; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.13 FR-BOM-01-14; supporting NFR-SEC-03,08, NFR-REL-03,05-06. Website: index.html loads app/pricing-state.js P.save, I.recipe and P.saveStaffRecipe, app/owner-products.js materialRecipe/material rows and combined product save, app/inventory-state.js recipe/material calculations and app/cake-data.js supported cake ingredients/configuration. Current XMLs reviewed, particularly BPMN-22/26/33/34. SRS is primary: show supported cake-option mappings even where website editor coverage is partial. Scope: recipe definition maintenance for one product variant or supported cake option and authorized read-only production reference. Recipes directly reference inventory base ingredients; no nested recipes/prepared-component inventory. Owner alone may create/change rows/quantities; Staff can view but is denied mutation. Authentication is upstream BPMN-26; role checked at load and commit. Each saved mapping may reference an ingredient also used in other recipes, with no global ingredient exclusivity. Recipe change does not consume/reserve stock, procure supplies, alter paid order material/amount snapshots or approve a new final price. Website also edits overhead in recipe/pricing UI: overhead, costing and price decisions remain BPMN-36, not expanded here. BPMN-22 uses recipe quantities for planning; BPMN-09/11 for reservation; BPMN-13 for production consumption. These are rule/data-consumer references, not calls of whole transactions when a definition is saved. All local validation/failure/recovery paths are on the main diagram. Internal roles use sequence flows within one pool; no external participant/message flow or broadcast is needed. Recoverable field/save conflicts return to explicit review, correction, reload/retry or stopping. Proposed consistent-save safeguards follow SRS reliability even if preview is only in-memory. Do not invent universal recipe version pinning or automatic recalculation/replacement of existing fulfillments.</bpmn:documentation>
